=== what this run says ===

  baseline                                          ALIVE
  after ONE fire at 0x300a                          ALIVE
  phase 1  read all 128 ArduChip registers, 3 times, NO fires ALIVE
  phase 2  36 writes of 0x07 = 0x00, no bits set    ALIVE
  phase 3  fire at the FIVE HIGH addresses, 3 visits (0x3000-0x3100) ALIVE
  phase 4  fire at the SEVEN LOW addresses, 3 visits (0x0000-0x001D) ALIVE
  phase 5  20260907-i2cpass's STAGE A, whole and unshortened ALIVE

  NOTHING BREAKS THE HANDLE - not the pieces and not stage A whole.
  20260907-i2cpass's dead control surface DOES NOT REPRODUCE, so the
  reading in that directory - that firing 0x07 bit 0 costs the manual
  exposure - is wrong, and its stage B failed for some other reason
  this run has not found. What is now unblocked is stage B itself: the
  handle is alive on both sides of a fire, which is the precondition it
  needed and never had.

